🧱 1. Sharing Rules – “The Basic Access Builder”

Scenario :
Sales Rep Maria owns an account called “Apple Tech” . She wants the North America Sales Manager to see all her accounts for review purposes.

What They Do :
They create a sharing rule :

Share all accounts owned by users in the “North America Sales Rep” role with the “North America Sales Manager” role — Read Only.

✅ Use Case: Simple ownership-based sharing across roles or groups.

⚙️ 2. Apex Managed Sharing – “The Custom Automation Hero”

Scenario :
TechGear has premium customers. Each has a Customer Success Manager (CSM) assigned via a custom field CSM__c. CSMs need access to their assigned accounts automatically.

What They Do :
A developer writes an Apex trigger that runs when the CSM field changes:

Automatically shares the account with the new CSM with Read/Write access.

✅ Use Case: When standard sharing rules can’t handle dynamic field-based sharing.

🌍 3. Territory Management – “The Regional Data Organizer”

Scenario :
TechGear expands globally. They want sales reps in Europe to only see European accounts. Their Regional Director should see all European accounts, and the VP of Sales should see everything.

What They Do :
Enable Territory Management :

Create territories: Europe, North America, Asia.
Assign users to appropriate territories.
Define hierarchy so higher-level users can see data from lower ones.
✅ Use Case: For large-scale geographic or segment-based access control.

👥 4. Teams – “The Collaboration Tool”

Scenario :
Maria closes a big deal with “Apple Tech” . She adds:

A Solution Engineer to the Opportunity Team.
A Legal Reviewer to ensure contract compliance.
A Customer Success Manager to the Account Team.
What They Do :
Use Opportunity Team and Account Team to give these users access to just that one record.

✅ Use Case: When specific people need access to individual records for collaboration.

🔁 5. Duplicate Rules – “The Data Quality Guardian”

Scenario :
Someone tries to create a new account named “Apple Tech” , but there’s already one in the system.

What They Do :
Create a Duplicate Rule on Account:

If Name matches exactly, show a warning or block creation.

Also add a Matching Rule :

Match if Name is similar, Phone matches, or Email matches.

✅ Use Case: Prevent duplicate records and maintain clean data.

